{#
    A statement a `datamodel="sce-static"` document's lowering wrote
    (`Action::native_code`, SCE Accepted Subset §2.15): Go reading and writing
    the policy's fields, with no script engine.

    One that can fail (`native_fails`: a checked integer operation) is not a
    statement but an expression that is `true` when it failed — the value is
    computed first and written only when it did not fail, so a failed statement
    leaves what it was going to write as it was. W3C SCXML 4.9: the error ends
    the block, which `return` leaves from the closure the block runs in, as it
    does for every other element that raised; `error.execution` was raised by
    the expression itself.
#}
{% if action.native_fails %}
	if {{ action.native_code }} {
{% if in_action_block is defined and in_action_block %}
		return  // W3C SCXML 4.9: the error ends the block
{% endif %}
	}
{% else %}
	{{ action.native_code }}
{% endif %}
